      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Now I also tried it with the new 3rd-person view and the change in avatar's posture is still clearly visible (especially when looking down). ~~One reason might be IK working in world space and scaling not affecting IK points and bones instantly as feet are going inward/outward while scaling. Making IK local space could potentially also fix arm/leg bending issues at small scales or in large worlds far from origin, but I'm not sure.~~\n\nEdit: I am not sure about what's the cause and what would be the correct solution as I heard another person has this issue but in VR. https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/jittering-view-effect-when-lerping-osc-avatar-scaling",
      "viewerReactions": null,
